[quote="phantaskippy"]

I think the biggest hurdle is the worldbuilding.&nbsp; If this story is in the US (or any major country) how did they get permission to do this?&nbsp; What do people think of it?I think there is a ton of potential for the idea, but I see it fitting an island or otherwise isolated location with a lot of autonomy that suddenly markets a &quot;perfect city&quot;, complete with disaster proof buildings and infrastructure, nearly instant repairs, perfect security, etc.&nbsp; The fact that they are using Omnitron tech would have to be the secret that the players will probably guess right away, but still have to deal with.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I don&#39;t think it is too hard to imagine getting permission. This tech could allow for large-scale rebuilding efforts with little threat to no threat to workers lives. And if we utilize Omni&#39;s recycling capabilities the it could potentially break the formula and be Fast, Cheap, and Good.

&nbsp;

The research was done privately, and now they want to use the tech, right after Oblivaeon leveled huge sections of the US and other countries. It is the perfect environment for this sort of tech to be greenlit, because if it works it changes the situation from apocalyptic to merely disastrous.

&nbsp;

Plus, you don&#39;t need to convince &quot;The US Government&quot; simply your local representatives who deal with the building codes. One person, in charge of the budget, offered a sweet deal in land purchased, people relocated, and all the credit for being the guy who allowed for this quick recovery. I think he&#39;s probably jumping on board.

&nbsp;

But, I hadn&#39;t considered the political angle before, so now I need to think about who this guy is and how big of a wave he&#39;s riding right now.

&nbsp;

[quote="Phantom5613"]

One more thing you have to deal with is the fact that Omnitron is still kind of around.If I&#39;m remembering the Omnitron episode of LPP right, the hero version of Omnitron(O-X) is now the sole version in the RPG timeline. Depending on how you decide to use him, he may react any number of ways to old Omni tech being used.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Yeah, but I feel like that is a down the road problem. O-X is stil recovering from his battle with Omnitron IV and Obvlivaeon, he&#39;s too distracted to make a fuss even if he feels like a fuss needs to be raised.

&nbsp;

He may actually approve, since it would represent a change where his ancestors descendants could be seen as the partners of humanity instead of their enemies.

&nbsp;

But, another good point I&#39;ll have on the back burner

[quote="Jeysie"]

&nbsp;
<div class="bb-quote"><b>MindWanderer wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">I would say mainly: don&#39;t overthink it.
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Honestly my own comments were less &quot;this makes no sense so don&#39;t do it&quot;, but more reading the &quot;there won&#39;t be complications at first&quot; bit and thinking that to me the entire fun of trying to come up with complex reasons for why a certain thing exists in the setting the way it does is because it gives you plot hooks and ways to make the players&#39; lives interesting. If you&#39;re not going to do that, then I feel you might as well go with something simpler and more reasonably ignorable.(Same with PC backstories; I like coming up with detailed &quot;why does my character do their thing&quot; because it makes it easier to roleplay them and easier for the PC to come up with plot hooks for you specifically.)But I agree with not making it merely &quot;Omnitron yet again&quot;; I was trying to come up with ways that an AI with insta-building capabilities could make life interesting for the PCs and NPCs without even necessarly being malevolent, merely weird and annoying.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Ah, when I said &quot;there won&#39;t be complications at first&quot; I really just meant I don&#39;t want it to be obvious right away. The players are the new hero team hired to protect the new city, The Crownsguard, but I want them comfortable with the city and potentially have solved a few outside threats before I fully reveal Brighid and her origns. Probably hint at her sooner, but I want this to be a mid-story twist sort of deal, not an initial salvo.

&nbsp;

Otherwise I completely agree, half the fun is finding ways to make things challenging, not just interesting.
